    "img:001": {
      "evidence_id": "img:001",
      "record_kind": "imaging",
      "title": "Inpatient X-ray contrast studies and special examinations",
      "clinical_time": "2124-08-01T07:31:18",
      "available_time": "2124-08-02T17:48:54",
      "content": "Bilateral heterogeneously dense breast tissue. A mass with calcification is present posteromedial to the left areola, assessed as BI-RADS category 4C. Scattered ring-shaped and punctate calcifications are present in both breasts and the left axilla, assessed as BI-RADS category 2. Please correlate with clinical physical examination and other examinations, with follow-up.\nNo obvious thickening of the skin or areolae of either breast is seen, and there is no nipple retraction. The structural layers of the subcutaneous adipose tissue are clear. The glandular tissue of both breasts is abundant and dense, showing patchy areas of increased density with bulging margins. A mass measuring approximately 2.1*4.8cm is present posteromedial to the left areola, with relatively smooth, well-defined margins and internal punctate calcifications. Scattered ring-shaped and punctate calcifications are present in both breasts and the left axilla. No clustered fine sand-like calcifications are seen. Bilateral axillary lymph nodes are visualized.",
      "direct_identifiers_removed": true
    },
    "img:002": {
      "evidence_id": "img:002",
      "record_kind": "imaging",
      "title": "Inpatient CT",
      "clinical_time": "2124-08-01T13:31:06",
      "available_time": "2124-08-05T17:54:52",
      "content": "Multiple small nodules in both lungs, mostly ground-glass nodules, with the dominant nodule being a ground-glass nodule in the superior lingular segment of the left upper lobe; a soft-tissue mass in the left breast. Please correlate with clinical findings and other relevant examinations and follow up.\nMultiple nodular opacities in both lungs. Among the subsolid nodules, a larger one is located in the superior lingular segment of the left upper lobe (SE203, IM111), with a long-axis diameter of approximately 5mm and a vacuole sign; another larger one is located in the anterior basal segment of the right lower lobe (SE203, IM144), with a long-axis diameter of approximately 5mm. Among the solid nodules, a larger one is located in the lateral basal segment of the right lower lobe (SE203, IM216), with a long-axis diameter of approximately 4mm; another larger one is located in the medial segment of the right middle lobe (SE203, IM126), with a long-axis diameter of approximately 4mm. No abnormalities are seen in either hilar region. The visualized tracheobronchial structures are normal. No abnormally enlarged lymph nodes are seen in the mediastinum. A nodular soft-tissue lesion is seen in the left breast, with a cross-sectional size of approximately 2.5mmX2.1mm.",
      "direct_identifiers_removed": true
    },
