      "title": "Inpatient MRI",
      "clinical_time": "2124-08-01T07:39:19",
      "available_time": "2124-08-05T17:49:43",
      "content": "Mass in the upper inner quadrant of the left breast; please correlate with contrast-enhanced breast MRI.\nNon-contrast scan: The skin surfaces of both breasts are smooth, with slight thickening of the medial skin of the left breast. There is no retraction of either nipple, and the subcutaneous tissue planes are clearly delineated. Both breasts have abundant dense glandular tissue with mildly disorganized architecture, generally symmetric. A mass is visible in the upper inner quadrant of the left breast, showing isointensity on T1W, slightly high signal intensity on FST2W, high signal intensity on DWI, and an ADC value of approximately 1.4×10-3mm2/s. A nodular shadow is seen in the lateral right breast (se302 img17), showing isointensity on T1W, slightly high signal intensity on FST2W, high signal intensity on DWI, and an ADC value of approximately 1.2×10-3mm2/s. No abnormal signal is seen in the retromammary spaces bilaterally. No obviously enlarged lymph nodes are seen in either axilla.",
